Verdict: No go, never buy that thing. Only if you are big fan of the AC then only after 4-5 paths at some sells for $15 tops.

I play DMC a few times and this game impressed me a lot. But here are my recommendations :
* Unless you REALLY love "Hack 'N' Slash" Games, give this a try. It's a good one;
* The PC port is bad, (like) really bad (suffering a few stutters, even with V-Sync on. Plus the cutscenes lags a lot [maybe it's the infamous "30/24fps lock" and forced graphics effects]);
* Don't have a "XBOX Controller"? "Poor you", I mean, it will be a problem, if you have a "Joystick Controller" like me or wanna just stick to the "Keyboard&Mouse" I had to use another program, to emulate my Controller (CupHead is one of the only games, I've seen my controller work. The rest is like "XInput ONLY");
* Pay attention to your configs (because if you are calibrating "keyboard&mouse" and forget to map all the keys and cancel the configs, you will not be able to do anything. Input system literally dies....);
* And don't forget, that this game has the "Wonder..." (awful) "Quick Time Events" x-x. Disabling the UI will make the chapter 2 (for example) impassable (sort of a bug, but why would anyone play without the UI?? It becomes soo.... whatsoever);
Pick this game on sale, because this port seems to be a "Ctrl-C | Ctrl-V" from XBOX-360 version to PC. Not only graphics are a problem, but a few other small points (like one, I described above).
(8/10) I like this game a lot and it's an excellent Hack 'N' Slash game. But it's  worth the half of the price, in this condition at least.

